# UNCR - Restore a crunched file

```text
UNCR [drive:]file [destination-drive:]
```

## Restore a file

```text
B0:UNCR A:REPORT.TZT D:
```

The CRUNCH header supplies the restored name. Use a destination drive
where that name is free. UNCR checks the additive checksum before
publishing the output and retains the compressed input.

## Historical files

UNCR reads supported CRUNCH 2.x streams, including those written by
[CR](CR.HLP). It rejects 1.x streams. Use [USQ](USQ.HLP) for squeezed
files and [UNLZH](UNLZH.HLP) for CrLZH files.
